1. POLICY CHECKPOINTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Twenty-nine policies, and every checkpoint they load is third-party. Nineteen
weight files are committed beside the policy that loads them; ./download_weights.sh
pulls fourteen from their upstream repositories, so you take those under the
upstream's terms rather than under this repository's; ./export_onnx.py converts
one on your machine. Five cannot be obtained automatically at all and are marked
"no automated path" below -- running those five policies means producing the file
yourself.

Some rows are ONNX conversions, written by ./export_onnx.py from the TorchScript
checkpoints above them so that a policy can run on TensorRT. A conversion is a
derivative of its source and carries the source's terms unchanged -- putting a
weight in another container grants no right that did not already exist. So each
conversion ships only where its source's terms allow it to: amo's and rl_gym's
are committed because their checkpoints are redistributable, and robomimic's is
generated on your machine because its checkpoint declares no licence at all.
The amo and rl_gym checkpoints themselves are fetched rather than committed --
that is a repository-size choice about PyTorch blobs, not a licence one, and it
does not affect their conversions.

The sha256 column is the first four hex of the file's sha256 -- an identifier
for this table, not an integrity check. `sha256sum policies/*/model*` gives the
real thing. The committed files verify against this record as committed, and
./download_weights.sh carries the full sha256 of every file it fetches and
refuses a download that does not match it.

